Explorer team,

The vault web reaches into Send in three places: read-only share tokens are transfers (vault-loader.js:157),
the check-token indicator calls /api/transfers/check-token, and public previews are transfer-backed (sg-link-card).
Q1, Q2 and Q9 in the pack ask whether these are vault features. Defaults if unanswered: no, no, keep-during-grace.

Follow-up that is yours whatever the answers: a native token registry inside the vault API (phase 2, step 2.1),
so hosted vaults.sgit.ai stops validating tokens against the Send Admin Lambda. Design brief in the phase-2 folder.

Also recorded for you, not fixed (Villager rule): F1–F7 in 05__open-questions.md §3.2 — CORS omits the enum-key header
in the container, MCP omits append routes and never forwards the write key, == on the write-key hash, the S3 root
duplicated in the CloudFront function, the append lane folder named with the raw token.

— architect.villager
